  "verbalization": "Esketamine is implicated in the targeting of Acyl-CoA hydrolase, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Tenuifolin F, Lehualide A, and Epicatechin-(4beta->6)-epicatechin-(4beta->8)-catechin. These compounds collectively interact with the Inner centromere protein, suggesting a potential pathway through which Esketamine may influence this protein. The evidence is supported by multiple high-scoring paths, indicating a consistent relationship across different targets. The mechanism appears to involve the interaction of Esketamine with a hydrolase enzyme, which is then targeted by various compounds, ultimately affecting the Inner centromere protein. This suggests a possible role in cellular processes related to centromere function, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of hydrolase enzymes in mediating the effects of Esketamine on chromosomal structures.",
